  "question": {
    "text": "Two polaroids&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are placed in such a way that the pass-axis of polaroids are perpendicular to each other. Now, another polaroid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is placed between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> bisecting angle between them. If intensity of unpolarised light is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> then intensity of transmitted light after passing through polaroid&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> will be :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YUVSi",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MuD7i",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gj3MQ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MxLfz",
      "text": "Zero",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/22691055-1072-4c41-ae32-2622b53d7ab2-9895925.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 282px;\" /></p><p>As given here, the pass axis of polaroids&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are inclined at angle of &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#186;</mo></math> with&nbsp;each other. Another polaroid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>is placed at angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>with&nbsp;respect to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>Therefore, intensity of light after falling on polaroid&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Intensity of light after falling on polaroid&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Intensity of light after falling on&nbsp;polaroid&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
